  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-SPS802</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the Caribbean Congress of Labour (CCL) in organizing its triennial congress and training delegates in November 2025. The CCL, designated as an associate institution of the Caribbean Community, faces resource disparities compared to the Caribbean Private Sector Organisation (CPSO). The ILO will assist the CCL in developing themes such as worker rights protection, occupational safety and health, labour administration systems, digitalization, artificial intelligence, climate change, and just transitions. Additionally, the ILO will support the 4th Biennial Caribbean Workers&#x2019; Forum, organized by the Elma Francois Institute for Research and Debate, to establish regional dialogue on labour issues and assess the impact of new paradigms on workers and their institutions.

Beneficiaries of these initiatives include trade unions, workers, and employers in the Caribbean, who will benefit from enhanced dialogue, training, and policy development. The work will be done in collaboration with the CCL, Cipriani College of Labour and Cooperative Studies, and other regional institutions. The ILO will also organize a subregional workshop to improve trade union participation in reporting on ratified conventions and enhance the strategic use of ILO Supervisory Mechanisms. Furthermore, the ILO will support the CCL in integrating into wider Latin American and Caribbean trade union networks and addressing issues of violence and harassment in the workplace.</narrative>
  </description>
